  "worked_solution": "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929099/recovery/assets/373ea8254a9816f67bfbcaf993348f409c1047284d09c43e5d41e68b15c5af58.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane. Therefore $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<arg\u2061(z)<\\pi .$ If $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan\u2061\\alpha  & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\alpha  & =arctan\u2061(\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\  & \u22480.927\\,30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg\u2061(z)\u2248\\pi -0.927\\,30\u22482.21\n$$\n\nto two decimal places.",
